    "body": "**Independent exact-HEAD code review: `940bc6152ea7f467788d0911c7b92bf55e33bb98` (2026-10-29).** Earlier issue with unconditional 88px lower-panel minimum is fixed in the diff. Verified 5-file scope and exact Web/docs mirror blob SHAs (`ui-core.js:56ab91bb…`, `style-base.css:43174fb…`). `ai-forensics-evidence` run #1978 / 40871086200 = SUCCESS; its job only compiles forensic scripts and publishes evidence, so it does **not** establish mobile/browser PASS. Draft/unmerged is appropriate.\n\n**New remaining edge case, please test before merge:** `ensureMobilePinnedChatLayout().sync` detects keyboard shrink, and its focusin listener explicitly covers `#chatInput, #dmInput, #reportInput`. But the new menu-close guard checks only `document.activeElement === #chatInput`. With a short visual viewport and the menu open when `#dmInput` (or `#reportInput`) has focus, the menu remains open, `chatCapacity` may reach 0, and the computed chat height can collapse even though a different editor is active. The runner's new short-viewport case exercises only `#chatInput`; the DM/report case is not covered. This is a **code-level gap / plausible overflow**, not a claim of visual reproduction.\n\nFollow-up **same Codex thread / same PR #431**: (1) specify intended behavior for DM/report editing while menu open, ensuring menu cannot starve the pinned chat and active panel; (2) extend the short-viewport fixture to DM/report focus, and where possible real DOM bounds / reflows, confirming keyboard/menu closed restoration; (3) execute the actual browser regression, ideally via local headless Chromium/Playwright against the working HTTP fixture as a fallback when Codex Browser transport is down; include precise PASS/FAIL logs. Preserve current `ui-mobile.js` authority and Web/docs byte parity. Do not touch PR #453, Stage7.15, Chat03 or other branches, do not merge or deploy.\n\nNote: `UI.hideMenu` from `ui-menu.js` does call `UI.ensureMobilePinnedChatLayout()` again, so the currently implemented chat-focus reentry itself is valid. Physical iPhone Safari owner acceptance remains separate.",
