    "body": "## Summary\n\n- Synced the existing branch with current `main@31b7a077820914e92de81239e5ab4099e3dfa558` using a non-force merge commit; resolved the real `ui-core.js` conflict in both mirrors.\n- Kept the current app's existing `mobilePanelTabs` / `ui-mobile.js` navigation as the single source for tab switching, gestures, long-press hints, accessibility, and panel scroll state.\n- Fixed short visual viewport allocation: chat and panel heights are bounded by the space actually available. When the keyboard is open, the chat input is focused, and the open menu prevents the composer and lower panel from fitting, the menu is closed through the existing `UI.hideMenu()` controller.\n- Extended the regression runner with a 320x568 fixture that starts with menu open and chat input focused, simulates a reduced visual viewport, checks actual input/chat/panel bounds and scroll areas, then checks keyboard/menu size restoration.\n- Prevented the open mobile Goal body from flex-shrinking to zero.\n\n## Scope\n\nOnly these five paths differ from current main:\n\n- `AsyncScene/Web/ui/ui-core.js`\n- `docs/ui/ui-core.js`\n- `AsyncScene/Web/style-base.css`\n- `docs/style-base.css`\n- `tools/test_mobile_shell_regressions.html`\n\nPR #453 remains untouched. No Chat03, Chat04.1 implementation, Stage 7.15, Cloudflare, or game mechanics changes are included.\n\n## Verification on exact HEAD `940bc6152ea7f467788d0911c7b92bf55e33bb98`\n\n- `python3 tools/test_mobile_first_interface_contract.py`: 14/14 PASS.\n- `node --check` for both UI-core mirrors and the regression runner script: PASS.\n- `git diff --check`: PASS.\n- Web/docs `ui-core.js` and `style-base.css`: byte-identical.\n- GitHub combined status and PR workflow runs: no checks/runs reported yet for this HEAD.\n- The expanded browser regression runner was not executed: Codex Desktop's browser inventory returned `transport closed before response` after reinitialization. The local loopback fixture server started successfully, but no browser visual PASS is claimed.\n- The runner uses a controlled `visualViewport` reduction; it does not synthesize a native OS keyboard. Physical iPhone/Safari acceptance remains user-owned.\n\nKeep this PR Draft. Run the browser fixture and request independent review before merge.",
